## 2.2 Materials characterization
Powder X-ray diffraction (XRD) data of samples were collected on Bruker D8 ADVANCE diffractometer system using $\mathrm{{Cu}\ K a}$ radiation of wavelength $\lambda=0.15,418\ \mathrm{nm}$ at room temperature. The simulated pattern was obtained from Materials Studio 7.0 package. $\Nu_{2}$ adsorption/desorption isotherms were measured at $77~\mathrm{K}$ on a Micromeritics’ ASAP 2460 calculating the Brunauer–Emmett–Teller (BET) surface area and pore size distribution at the same time. Before the sorption measurements, all the samples were outgassed for $^{4\mathrm{~h~}}$ at $423\mathrm{~K~}$ . Scanning electron microscope (SEM) was examined on a ZEISS Ultra 55 instrument at a low landing energy $(5.0\mathrm{kV})$ . Transmission electron microscope (TEM) images were revealed on an electron microscope (JEM-2100HR) at operated energy of $200\ensuremath{\mathrm{\kV}}$ . Thermogravimetry (TGA) was performed on a TG 209 instrument (Netzsch) and the samples were heated under nitrogen atmosphere from 298 up to $1173\mathrm{~K~}$ at a rate of $5~\mathrm{K~min^{-1}}$ . The gaseous toluene adsorption experiment was performed on an intelligent gravimetric analyzer (3H2000PW, Beishide Instrument Technology (Beijing)), and all ZIF-90 samples were outgassed for $6\mathrm{~h~}$ at $423\mathrm{~K~}$ before the test.
